LRC(14) OPEN-Q-108 THREAD 2 -- THE EXTREMAL PRINCIPLE  (kind-pasteur-kpswf2)
Is 'AP maximizes corr' reducible to 'AP maximizes K-weighted support-3'?


==================================================================================
PART A -- the SUPPORT-6 FLOOR (Lemma A): does support-3 carry ANY K-weight?
==================================================================================
  Claim (S9-wf Lemma A): K(n)=0 unless n has >=6 nonzero non-7 coords.
  If true, the K-WEIGHTED support-3 (and -2,-4,-5) enumerator is IDENTICALLY 0,
  so 'AP maximizes corr via support-3' is mechanistically vacuous.

   support s       max |K(n)| over random non-7 relations
           1                                    2.944e-16  <- ZERO (annihilated)
           2                                    6.939e-17  <- ZERO (annihilated)
           3                                    9.248e-18  <- ZERO (annihilated)
           4                                    1.900e-18  <- ZERO (annihilated)
           5                                    2.914e-20  <- ZERO (annihilated)
           6                                    1.557e-06  <- NONZERO (carries weight)
           7                                    1.261e-07  <- NONZERO (carries weight)

  => SUPPORT-6 FLOOR holds: True
     CONSEQUENCE: corrS(E,3) = 0 exactly.  The signal lives at support>=6.

