==================================================================================
PART C (k=7) -- ADVERSARIAL: exhaustive argmax of corr over k-subsets of [0,N]
==================================================================================
  Does the AP/consec UNIQUELY maximize corr among ALL k-subsets in a window?
  (the classical 'AP maximizes additive energy' analog, now for the SIGNED corr).

  N=  9:    120 subsets;  max corr = 0.25783 at (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)
         consec_7 corr = 0.14150;  a consecutive block is argmax: True
         #argmax ties = 1
  N= 11:    792 subsets;  max corr = 0.25783 at (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)
         consec_7 corr = 0.14150;  a consecutive block is argmax: True
         #argmax ties = 1
  N= 13:   3432 subsets;  max corr = 0.25783 at (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)
         consec_7 corr = 0.14150;  a consecutive block is argmax: True
         #argmax ties = 1

  (corr is DILATION-invariant: meas(S7(c*E))=meas(S7(E)); so all dilates of consec
   tie.  The question is whether any NON-dilate-of-AP set beats them.)

==================================================================================
PART D (k=8) -- structured non-AP families vs AP (the signed-cancellation risk)
==================================================================================
  Classical fact: AP maximizes additive energy E(A). Structured 'almost-AP' sets
  (dilated APs, 2-D GAPs, unions of APs) have HIGH energy too. Does the SIGNED
  K-weight ever let one BEAT the AP on corr (cancellation working FOR them)?

  AP/consec corr = 0.302731

                  family        corr     corr-AP  beats AP?
               consec AP    0.302731   +0.000000      False
           2*AP (dilate)    0.302731   +0.000000      False
              AP+1 shift    0.320418   +0.017687       True
              GAP 2 rows    0.070650   -0.232081      False
              GAP 3 rows    0.302731   +0.000000      False
     union 2 APs (step2)    0.029489   -0.273243      False
           AP one defect    0.183854   -0.118878      False
          AP two defects    0.017187   -0.285544      False
              B2 (Sidon)   -0.012358   -0.315090      False

  => any structured non-AP set BEATS the AP on corr: True

